Claude Code ships a browser integration for Chrome. firefox-use exposes the
same tool names and the same parameters for Firefox, so a browser task written
for one runs on the other. Names and parameter shapes are an interface, and
they are matched deliberately; the prose - every tool description, the skill,
the documentation - is written for this project.

Anthropic's own tool definitions are not redistributed here.
`scripts/extract-chrome-spec.js` reads them out of the Claude Code install on
your own machine to produce a local test fixture (`.spec/`, never committed),
which `test/parity.test.js` compares our schemas against. Running it requires
your own licensed copy of Claude Code, and nothing it produces leaves your
machine.

